---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import AiLandingHero from '../components/AiLandingHero.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { describeServiceHref } from '../data/contact';

const context = 'AI-assisted implementation';
---

<Base
  title="Implement and adapt a public service | Registry Stack"
  description="Adapt open-source registry software to your forms, rules and systems. Work with our team to configure and test one service in a scoped pilot."
>
  <SiteHeader current="customization" />
  <main>
    <AiLandingHero
      eyebrow="AI-assisted implementation"
      heading="Build a service around your rules."
      lead="Adapt open-source registry software to your forms, rules and review steps. Our team uses AI to help prepare changes your institution can review and test before approving them."
      context={context}
      exampleHref="#change-example"
      exampleLabel="See a change example"
      note="Available through a scoped implementation pilot."
    >
      <p class="ai-example-label">Proposed change</p>
      <p class="ai-example-title">Open enrolment to five-year-olds</p>
      <dl class="ai-example-rows">
        <div><dt class="ai-example-label">Entry age</dt><dd>6 years to <strong>5 years</strong></dd></div>
        <div><dt class="ai-example-label">Turns five by the cut-off</dt><dd>Meets the age rule</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="ai-example-label">Turns five after the cut-off</dt><dd>Does not meet the age rule</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </AiLandingHero>

    <section class="section section-muted" id="change-example" aria-labelledby="change-title">
      <div class="section-inner approach-split">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Illustrative school enrolment</p>
          <h2 id="change-title">Change one rule across the whole service</h2>
          <p>An education authority lowers the entry age for pre-primary school. That affects what the service checks, what staff tell parents and what appears in the assignment notice.</p>
          <p>Our team can use AI to help draft the changes. The education authority reviews the proposed behavior and test results before approving a release.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="editorial-callout">
          <h3>What the team checks before release</h3>
          <dl class="change-checks">
            <div><dt>Eligibility</dt><dd>The service applies the cut-off date for the correct school year.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Evidence</dt><dd>An approved age check uses the revised rule and has an agreed fallback.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Notice</dt><dd>The assignment letter names the right programme and start date.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Guidance</dt><dd>The portal and school office give parents the same information.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="how-customization-works" aria-labelledby="pilot-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="pilot-title">What you agree in an implementation pilot</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="value-grid">
          <article>
            <h3>Fit with your existing systems</h3>
            <p>We assess where reusable records, forms or review steps can help. Together we agree what to configure, which systems to connect and where the service will run.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Cases to try before going live</h3>
            <p>Try a typical request and an exception. Check what people can see, who records the decision and who can make the resulting change.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>What your team will take over</h3>
            <p>Agree which configuration, tests and operating instructions your team receives, and who will run the service and maintain each connection. The configured service can run without an AI model.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="section-note">Still defining the service? <a href="/ai/service-design/">See how to prepare a service brief</a>. You can also <a href="/starters/">browse starting configurations</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="proof-title">
      <div class="section-inner approach-split">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Released example</p>
          <h2 id="proof-title">Try a licence status check</h2>
          <p>In this separate Evidence Gateway example, a request with one matching active licence gets a signed answer. The sample cases show what happens if two licences match or the source is unavailable.</p>
          <a class="inline-cta" href="https://github.com/registrystack/registry-stack/tree/v0.46.0/products/evidence/examples/standalone/">Explore the runnable example with fictional data <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <section id="studio" class="editorial-callout" aria-labelledby="studio-title">
          <p class="eyebrow">In development</p>
          <h3 id="studio-title">Registry Studio</h3>
          <p>We’re building a workspace for reviewing suggested requirements and tracking questions for your team. An assistant for proposing changes directly in Studio is planned.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="final-cta" aria-labelledby="next-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2 id="next-title">Scope one implementation pilot</h2>
        <p>Bring a public form and a fictional example of what you need to change. We’ll discuss what to build and test. Tell us about any limits on AI tools or data use.</p>
        <div class="section-links">
          <a class="button button-primary" href={describeServiceHref(context)} data-journey="service-inquiry">Discuss your service</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/pricing/">View implementation options</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .change-checks { margin: 0; }
  .change-checks > div { border-top: 1px solid var(--registry-paper-rule); padding: 10px 0; }
  .change-checks > div:last-child { padding-bottom: 0; }
  .change-checks dt { color: var(--registry-ink); font-weight: 700; }
  .change-checks dd { line-height: 1.5; margin: 2px 0 0; }
  #studio { scroll-margin-top: 78px; }
</style>
